                USING THE GUIDE TO EOTL
 
The guide has a number of handy uses for the beginner at EotL.
You can pick one up by buying one from the magic vending 
machine found in the EotL players' lounge, where you start 
upon the creation of your character.  After purchasing the 
guide, you might want to type 'info guide' to learn more about 
its features.  For your information, some of the most useful 
features are:
 
'query'        Query allows you to compare a foe (monster or player) 
               to you in terms of cumulative ability.  A threat level 
               1.000 is the same as you, the higher the number, the 
               harder it will be for you.  Each query costs you 5 
               mana points.
 
'beam me up'   This command allows you to "beam" back to the 
               Heart of Eternal City at a cost of some mana,
               depending on your level.
 
'Dest corpse'  This command will get rid of the corpses of the 
               monsters you kill, which reduces clutter and 
               clears game resources which, in turn, reduces lag
               which is nicer for you.
 
'stupor'       As a newbie player (which the guide will 
               determine), you are allowed to use the guide 
               to 'stupor.'  This exchanges unused fatigue 
               points for hit points, when you're in a bind. 
